States
======

State               Waits for (expect)  Action                                     Next
------------------  ------------------  -----------------------------------------  -------
state_login_telnet  /login: $/          send user                                  pw
                    /Password: $/       send_secret pass                           show
pw                  /Password: $/       send_secret pass                           show
show                prompt              send "show running-config"                 capture
capture             prompt              capture_start on entry, then capture_stop  logout
logout              (standalone send)   send "exit"                                done

States with more than one expect try them in order; the first match wins.

Template source
===============

Full source of templates/parks.tmpl:

    # parks.tmpl - Parks (Fiberlink) over telnet.
    #
    # syntax_style: cisco-ios
    #
    # Derived from fetchconfig::model::Parks. No enable, no pager; the show command
    # is fixed ("show running-config").
    # Note: DRAFT - please verify on real hardware.
    
    transport      telnet
    banner_timeout 30
    fetch_timeout  120
    max_visits     8
    
    # drop the echoed "show running-config" command line
    skip_first     1
    
    prompt_head    ''
    prompt_tail    '# $'
    
    # ---- telnet entry: interactive login ----
    state state_login_telnet
        expect /login: $/    -> send user        -> goto pw
        expect /Password: $/ -> send_secret pass   -> goto show
    
    state pw
        expect /Password: $/ -> send_secret pass   -> goto show
    
    state show
        expect prompt        -> send "show running-config" -> goto capture
    
    state capture
        capture_start
        expect prompt        -> capture_stop       -> goto logout
    
    state logout
        send "exit" -> done

